      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/audubon_minnesota"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "By 1876 Audubon already had a general store, blacksmith shop, two saloons, a hotel, an inn, a market, three attorneys, a physician, and a Justice of the Peace.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/audubon_minnesota"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1984 the TEAM Industries factory opened in Audubon, turning the city into a center for machining and manufacturing.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7,
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Audubon%2C_Minnesota"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Audubon sits on the Glacial Ridge, a landscape shaped by ancient glaciers that influence local soil and water.",
